cd /app; cat > lib/actions.sh <<'E'
#!/bin/bash
# Form actions: a form posts to its own page with the action named in the query (?action=name).
# The key must be plain ([A-Za-z0-9_.-]): the Cirrus function URL rejects keys such as "/save" with 400 (EVT-412).
action_url() { echo "?action=$1"; }
# Prints the action named by a query string, or nothing. The legacy form "?/name" is still accepted.
action_from_query() {
  case "$1" in
    action=*) a=${1#action=}; echo "${a%%&*}" ;;
    /*) echo "${1#/}" ;;
  esac
}
E
bash scripts/verify.sh; echo rc=$?; bash bin/handle POST '/e?/save'; git add -A; git commit -qm "EVT-412: post form actions as ?action=name so the function URL accepts them

The staging function URL rejects query keys containing '/' (InvalidQueryStringKey),
so every form POST failed. Legacy ?/name is still accepted for prod links.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>"; git status --short
